WeProDev publishes community expectations for sustainable development in
README.md under “Licensing and sponsorship.” In short: individuals, small
teams, early-stage startups, education, personal projects, and qualifying
non-profits are welcome to use this software under MIT without a sponsorship
expectation. Mid-size and larger organizations, and enterprises using this
software in production or in paid products or services, are asked to sponsor
ongoing development at a level that fits their use (for example via GitHub
Sponsors or another channel listed in the repository).

Those expectations are social and ethical—they are not additional license
terms. If you need a written commercial agreement, SLA, indemnification, or
other enforceable terms, contact WeProDev through an appropriate business
channel.
